; An array-of-`any` type-choice arm (`[* any] / tstr`) is a SUPPORTED rust position under
; --wasm=false: `[* any]` is a homogeneous array whose CBOR wire type (Array) is distinct from
; `tstr` (Text), so the ordinary choice machinery dispatches it correctly and it round-trips
; byte-exact (element lowered to `AnyCbor`, loose-CBOR A2). Under the catalog's default --wasm=true
; profile an any-using spec gracefully rejects (wasm is A3), so this row is `error (graceful)`, not
; the panic it formerly produced in generation/serialize.rs. DISTINCT from the bare-`any` arm
; (`any / tstr`, tests/robustness/choice_any_arm.cddl), which is rejected in EVERY profile because
; bare `any` overlaps every arm.
a = [* any] / tstr
